# Accepted, tracked base-image vulnerabilities. Our own code and dependencies still
# hard-fail the scan — these exceptions are ONLY for the distroless base image.
#
# All of these are openssl (libssl3) CVEs in the distroless base. Debian has published a
# fix, but the distroless base has not been rebuilt with it yet, and distroless has no
# package manager, so we cannot patch openssl ourselves from the Dockerfile. Blocking
# every deploy on an upstream base CVE outside our control is not viable; we accept these
# explicitly and delete each line once the base image ships the fix.
#
# Reviewed: 2026-09-06. Revisit on the next base-image bump.
# Production hardening: automate base rebuilds (Renovate) or use an aggressively-patched
# base (e.g. Chainguard), plus a real risk-acceptance workflow instead of a flat file.
CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2026-28387
CVE-2026-28388
CVE-2026-28389
